Z||000009||ITB 2M4||12-24-2001||09:56 PM||||Momo was once owned by Gianpierro Morretti, who used to race in the IMSA GTP/PSR WSC series.  His cars were always in the Momo colors, but never the same design from race to race!  He also used to be part of an indoor karting place in St. Pete, but that went belly up.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4<BR>AOL IM- DGPFiero||||reg||10
Z||000010||TRiAD||12-24-2001||10:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>ALL F-1 cars use MOMO wheels</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Uh, no. MOST use OZ Racing, one uses Fondmetal, and there are one or two other suppliers. One of them might be MOMO, but I'm unaware of them having wheels in F1. Even the MOMO-sponsored Ferrari 333SP in GT Sportscar racing used OZ Racing wheels. <BR>If you meant <I>steering</I> wheels, most use Sparco. <P><B> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>very high end stuff if ricers use it they have good sence<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That part (although misspelled) is true. <BR>||||reg||1
